welsh writer ken follett has come to  cologne from london bringing the drizzle  along with him  just in time to mark the 25th  anniversary of the fall of the berlin  wall he unveils a present from his  german publisher  it's an original piece of the wall  painted like the cover of the german  edition of his latest book  the novel deals with the cold war the  era in which the wall still stood  separating the opposing eastern and  western blocks i remember the fall of  the wall and what i remember about that  is that we didn't believe it was  permanent  you know sitting in london  or and  the same for people who are in the  united states  uh  we saw this happening and we thought yes  but tomorrow the tanks will arrive  uh because we  you know we had seen this before in  hungary in czechoslovakia and poland  where there had been a kind of rebellion  against the  the uh communist system but in the end  the rebellion had been crushed and a lot  of us thought that the same thing was  bound to happen again  for edge of eternity ken follett did  lots of research on location  the book intertwines the stories of five  families from the us and europe much of  the action takes place in divided berlin  there are several scenes in edge of  eternity  where somebody tries to escape  and of course that kind of scene is all  about the physical detail you know how  high is the wall how far do they have to  jump  or or what is the barrier like that they  have to crash through  and all of that stuff  those details are terribly important um  and that was quite difficult to research  because  happily for all of us the wall is no  longer there  for the last 35 years the former  journalist has written one bestseller  after another ken follett's books have  sold around 130 million copies worldwide  i always wanted to be a star  right from a young age and uh you know  when i was very young i didn't care what  kind of star i just wanted to be a star  you know authors aren't supposed to say  that author's supposed to had a message  to give the world  and  it wasn't like that for me it wasn't  like that for me i wanted to entertain  people i wanted them to love my story  follett's latest novels end his century  trilogy which began with fall of giants  and winter of the world in edge of  eternity he follows the stories of the  same families whose fates are closely  linked to world history  well my stories are about quite  fundamental things that affect everybody  uh i i write about wars and revolutions  but also about love and marriage  and raising children  the the the dramas in my books are  things i think that most people can  identify with  and his fans just can't get enough  pollets readings are sold out affairs  like here in cologne the celebrity  author can't resist divulging  interesting tidbits  mimi alford  recently wrote a book about her affair  with president kennedy she kept the  secret for 50 years  she's an old lady now  and so i sent her an email and said  would you be one of my consultants  and she read the scenes in which the  young woman  goes to bed with president kennedy  and she made some corrections and she  gave me some additional information  followed  whose family comes from east germany  i told him things about my history and  my parents about how he lived in east  germany and how my parents prepared to  flee  he made some notes in his book and at  the end he told me i wrote down every  word you said i wrote down every word  you said  ken follett's next book is already in  the works  he plans to take his readers on another  trip back in time with a spy thriller  about the beginnings of the british  secret service in the 16th century
 

